course: dictionary
lesson: 8721
title: Short forms and word parts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A short form is a shorter way of writing a word. Sep is short for September, the ninth month of the year. You will see it on calendars, tickets and food labels, and some writers use Sept instead.
explain: The dot in Sep. shows that letters have been left out. In notes, Sep. can be a short form of «separate», so the words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: A lower-case sep with no dot is usually a piece of a longer word, not a word on its own. Look for little words hidden inside big ones: «Separate» has «a rat» in it: sep-a-rat-e.
fact: Sep and Sep. are short forms of September, the ninth month.
fact: «Sep» on a calendar means September.
fact: Some writers use «Sept» instead of «Sep».
fact: Sep. can be a short form of «separate» in notes.
fact: Little helpers live inside big words: «definitely» has «finite» in the middle (de-finite-ly).
exercise: «Sep» on a calendar means which month? | Sunday | *September | December | Summer
exercise: In a note, «Sep.» might stand for which word? | Second | Seven | Sepia | *Separate
exercise: Find the little word hidden inside «definitely». | dinner | defy | lean | *finite
test: Which is a short form of September? | Sup | Spt | Sen | *Sep
test: «Separate» has which little word inside it? | a mat | *a rat | a cap
exam: Mia sees «Sep» on a ticket. What does it mean? | *September | Separate | Second | Sepia
